For automated pipelines (user-generated content sites, game asset farms, procedural batches):
// Meshy API example (text-to-3D)
const r = await fetch('https://api.meshy.ai/v2/text-to-3d', {
method: 'POST',
headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${MESHY_API_KEY}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
body: JSON.stringify({
mode: 'preview',
prompt: 'a low-poly mushroom, vibrant colours',
art_style: 'cartoon',
})
});
const { result: taskId } = await r.json();
// poll until ready
const model = await pollUntilReady(taskId);
const glbUrl = model.model_urls.glb;
// load into Three.js
const gltf = await new GLTFLoader().loadAsync(glbUrl);
scene.add(gltf.scene);
Tripo, Luma, Hunyuan have similar REST + polling APIs. TripoSR runs entirely on your own GPU — no external API.

import { init, threeToSoloNavMesh } from '@recast-navigation/three';
await init(); // load WASM
// gather meshes that the NavMesh should consider as ground / obstacles
const sources = [];
scene.traverse((c) => { if (c.isMesh && c.userData.walkable) sources.push(c); });
const { navMesh, success } = threeToSoloNavMesh(sources, {
cs: 0.2, // cell size (smaller = more detail, slower build)
ch: 0.2, // cell height
walkableSlopeAngle: 60,
walkableHeight: 2,
walkableClimb: 0.9,
walkableRadius: 0.6,
maxEdgeLen: 12,
maxSimplificationError: 1.3,
minRegionArea: 8,
mergeRegionArea: 20,
});
if (!success) throw new Error('NavMesh build failed');

import { NavMeshQuery } from 'recast-navigation';
const query = new NavMeshQuery({ navMesh });
const start = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };
const goal = { x: 10, y: 0, z: 8 };
const { path, success } = query.computePath(start, goal);
// path = array of waypoints
Visualise the path:
const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry().setFromPoints(path.map(p => new THREE.Vector3(p.x, p.y, p.z)));
const line = new THREE.Line(geo, new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({ color: 0xff00ff }));
scene.add(line);

Each frame, advance toward the next waypoint at walking speed; pop the waypoint when reached.
let pathIdx = 0;
const speed = 3;
useFrame ((s, dt) => {
if (pathIdx >= path.length) return;
const target = new THREE.Vector3(path[pathIdx].x, path[pathIdx].y, path[pathIdx].z);
const dir = target.clone().sub(character.position);
const d = dir.length();
if (d < 0.1) { pathIdx++; return; }
character.position.add(dir.normalize().multiplyScalar(speed * dt));
character.lookAt(target);
});

For many AI characters, Detour Crowd handles avoidance between them:
import { Crowd } from 'recast-navigation';
const crowd = new Crowd({ maxAgents: 200, maxAgentRadius: 0.6, navMesh });
const agent = crowd.addAgent({ x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 }, {
radius: 0.6, height: 2, maxAcceleration: 8, maxSpeed: 4,
});
agent.requestMoveTarget({ x: 10, y: 0, z: 0 });
useFrame((s, dt) => {
crowd.update(dt);
character.position.copy(agent.position());
});
For dynamic scenes (rebuild NavMesh as the world changes), use tiled NavMesh via threeToTiledNavMesh — only rebuild affected tiles.

npm install simplex-noise
import { createNoise2D } from 'simplex-noise';
const noise2D = createNoise2D();
const SIZE = 100;
const SEG = 200;
const geo = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(SIZE, SIZE, SEG, SEG);
const pos = geo.attributes.position;
for (let i = 0; i < pos.count; i++) {
const x = pos.getX(i);
const y = pos.getY(i);
const h = noise2D(x * 0.05, y * 0.05) * 5
+ noise2D(x * 0.2, y * 0.2) * 1
+ noise2D(x * 1.0, y * 1.0) * 0.25;
pos.setZ(i, h);
}
geo.computeVertexNormals();
const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x668866, flatShading: true }));
mesh.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;
scene.add(mesh);
Layering noise at multiple frequencies + amplitudes (fractal Brownian motion) gives natural-looking terrain.

